Tech notes: Our JS + Python SDKs support streaming and function calls. Browser: SSE; server: websocket. Function calls arrive as stream chunks with type="function_call" and args as JSON. For schema enforcement we recommend sending a JSON Schema in the system prompt and validating on the client when you receive the final assembled JSON. Example SSE snippet: ```js
const es = new EventSource('\nhttps://api.redwood.ai/v1/chat/stream?model=redwood-13b', { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${KEY}` } });
es.onmessage = (e) => { const chunk = JSON.parse(e.data); if (chunk.type === 'function_call') { handle(chunk.name, chunk.args); } };
```

