exactly — easiest implementation: store seq in cache entry and perform a metadata check on cache-populate for READ_STRONG prefixes. When eviction happens, and a reader triggers repopulate, the repopulate path validates seq against meta and refuses to write older seq. pseudocode:
```
// on repopulate for READ_STRONG
obj, seq = fetch_from_store(prefix)
meta_seq = meta_kv.get(prefix)
if seq < meta_seq:
  // another writer already advanced; fetch again or fail-through
  obj, seq = fetch_from_store(prefix) // retry once
cache.write(prefix, obj, seq)
```

