We do in a couple places, but not everywhere. Current behavior: check cache -> if kid present verify -> else fail. Improvement: on kid-miss perform one immediate fetch of JWKS (non-blocking retries with backoff) and re-check. Also guard with a short-circuit TTL so we don't DDOS the idp during a large burst. Pseudocode:
```
if (!jwks.has(kid)) {
  if (!recentRefreshInProgress) {
    fetch_jwks_immediate()
  }
  // re-check after fetch (synchronous wait up to 500ms) then continue
}
```
We should also log a metric when we see kid-miss so customer support can correlate.

